# Hover Color & Area Label UX Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** Make hover fill and area labels mode-aware — disabled fill + hover-only labels in editor, subtle fill + zoom-adaptive labels in preview/map.

**Architecture:** Add a `viewMode: "editor" | "preview" | "map"` prop to `useFloorPlanLayer` and `useFloorPlanLabels`. The highlight suppression and paint override live in `useFloorPlanLayer`; the draw-loop branching and zoom listener live in `useFloorPlanLabels`. Consuming components pass the correct viewMode and forward `hoveredAreaId` / `buildingName` as needed.

**Tech Stack:** TypeScript 5, React 19, MapLibre 5, Zustand 5, Next.js 16

## Global Constraints

- Do not add any new npm dependencies
- Do not modify the Zustand store shape (`useMapStore.ts`)
- `FloorPlanRenderMode` ("flat" | "3d") already exists on `useFloorPlanLayer` as `mode` — the new prop must be named `viewMode` to avoid collision
- All TypeScript must pass `npx tsc --noEmit` with zero new errors
- ESLint must pass with `npx eslint src/lib/map src/components/editor`
- Commit after every task

---

## File Map

| File | Role in this change |
|---|---|
| `src/lib/map/layer-definitions.ts` | Add two new exported constants for subtle hover fill |
| `src/lib/map/useFloorPlanLayer.ts` | Add `viewMode` prop; suppress highlight & override paint per mode |
| `src/lib/map/useFloorPlanLabels.ts` | Add `viewMode`, `hoveredAreaId`, `buildingName` props; branch draw loop; add zoom listener |
| `src/components/editor/Editor3DMapView.tsx` | Pass `viewMode="editor"` + `hoveredAreaId` to both hooks |
| `src/components/editor/PreviewOverlay.tsx` | Pass `viewMode="preview"` + `buildingName`; add name-gate to mousemove |

